{"hits": {"hits": [{"created": "2026-10-17T04:13:19.790607+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-17T04:13:20.322593+00:00", "id": 23430050, "conceptrecid": "23430049", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23430050", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23430049", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23430050", "metadata": {"title": "Two Seymour vertices in every sink-free oriented graph", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23430050", "publication_date": "2026-10-17", "description": "<p>We prove, relative to two explicitly stated results of the pinned OpenAI manuscript on Seymour's conjecture, that every nonempty finite sink-free oriented graph has two distinct vertices whose exact second out-neighborhood is at least as large as their first. This is Conjecture 2 of Dara, Francis, Jacob and Narayanan. The inputs are the ordinary one-vertex Seymour theorem and a finite-relation pruning lemma; their truth is stipulated here. A minimum counterexample has a unique good vertex with one successor. Deleting that vertex leaves weak subset deficits together with a strict inequality for subsets that do not reach the successor in one or two steps. In a transitive blowup, compatibility with the diagonal selects many fibers with this strict inequality. Their total gain dominates the possible losses of all remaining fibers, allowing the established pruning objective to close. All deductions from the two inputs are proved below. Finite diagnostics and formal supporting lemmas are distinguished from the full graph theorem.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>This is an AI-assisted preprint with internal independent agent reviews, not external peer review. The two stated OpenAI/math inputs at revision fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb are stipulated premises. The contribution comparison is bounded. Eleven Lean supporting theorems certify boundary, aggregation and conditional cardinality/pruning implications; the full graph theorem is not formalized. Paper and original prose CC BY 4.0; original code and Lean MIT.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Kang, Myeongjin", "affiliation": null}], "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23430049"}}]}}, "title": "Two Seymour vertices in every sink-free oriented graph", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23430050", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23430050", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23430050?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23430050", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23430050", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23430050", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23430050/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23430049", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23430049", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23430049", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23430049", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23430050/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23430050/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23430050/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23430050/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23430050:main.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23430050:main.pdf/full/%5E50,/0/default.jpg", "100": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23430050:main.pdf/full/%5E100,/0/default.jpg", "250": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23430050:main.pdf/full/%5E250,/0/default.jpg", "750": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23430050:main.pdf/full/%5E750,/0/default.jpg", "1200": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23430050:main.pdf/full/%5E1200,/0/default.jpg"}, "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23430050/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23430050/latest", "versions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23430050/versions", "draft": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23430050/draft", "access_links": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23430050/access/links", "access_grants": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23430050/access/grants", "access_users": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23430050/access/users", "access_request": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23430050/access/request", "access": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23430050/access", "communities": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23430050/communities", "communities-suggestions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23430050/communities-suggestions", "request_deletion": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23430050/request-deletion", "file_modification": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23430050/file-modification", "quota_increase": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23430050/quota-increase", "requests": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23430050/requests"}, "updated": "2026-10-17T04:13:20.322593+00:00", "recid": "23430050", "revision": 3, "files": [{"id": "558c6b4a-aca4-46c9-803a-258c9e557534", "key": "main.pdf", "size": 96943, "checksum": "md5:228c19bdcd3d7fc4c1b85879768c7859", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23430050/files/main.pdf/content"}}, {"id": "f02e8a84-7eb5-490d-9ec3-08fc8d973c60", "key": "r028-two-seymour-vertices-v1.zip", "size": 355950, "checksum": "md5:f58eab93cbb611ecaaf395a8111b04a7", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23430050/files/r028-two-seymour-vertices-v1.zip/content"}}], "swh": null, "owners": [{"id": "1931625"}], "status": "published", "stats": {"downloads": 4, "unique_downloads": 4, "views": 2, "unique_views": 1, "version_downloads": 4, "version_unique_downloads": 4, "version_unique_views": 1, "version_views": 2}, "state": "done", "submitted": true}, {"created": "2026-10-10T04:43:24.949228+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-12T03:53:34.718937+00:00", "id": 23274166, "conceptrecid": "23274165", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23274166", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23274165", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23274166", "metadata": {"title": "Dimension- and label-uniform stability of Gaussian propellers", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23274166", "publication_date": "2026-10-10", "description": "<p>Assume the sharp finite Gaussian propeller inequality and its finite equality classification. We prove that the deficit in the squared first-moment functional controls the square of the Gaussian measure distance to a propeller, with one positive constant independent of the ambient dimension and the number of cells. Cells may have arbitrarily small measure, and no masses are prescribed. The proof passes to countable Gaussian score arrays, excludes infinite-support equality cases, and bounds the gain from all additional scores by the three-halves power of their total squared norm and the squared common mean of the leading triple. A quadratic estimate for that triple and a Gaussian margin bound then give the partition estimate. The square-root dependence of distance on deficit is sharp already for three planar sectors. The universal constant is positive but implicit.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Kang, Myeongjin", "affiliation": "Independent researcher"}], "keywords": ["Gaussian partitions", "propeller conjecture", "stability", "Gaussian processes"], "version": "1", "references": ["S. Heilman, Euclidean partitions optimizing noise stability, Electron. J. Probab. 19 (2014), no. 71, 1\u201337. https://www.stevenheilman.org/~heilman/papers/SSC.pdf, Lemma 2.8.", "S. Heilman, A. Jagannath and A. Naor, Solution of the propeller conjecture in R^3, Discrete Comput. Geom. 50 (2013), 263\u2013305. https://doi.org/10.1007/s00454-013-9530-0. The uniqueness input is Remark 1.4 in the https://web.math.princeton.edu/~naor/homepage%20files/PropR3.pdf.", "S. Khot and A. Naor, Approximate kernel clustering, Mathematika 55 (2009), 129\u2013165. https://doi.org/10.1112/S002557930000098X.", "OpenAI, The Gaussian propeller bound in every dimension, September 24, 2026, preprint in the openai/math repository, revision fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb, https://github.com/openai/math/tree/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/The-Gaussian-Propeller-Bound-in-Every-Dimension-September-24-2026."], "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23274165"}}]}}, "title": "Dimension- and label-uniform stability of Gaussian propellers", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23274166", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23274166", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23274166?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23274166", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23274166", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23274166", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23274166/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23274165", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23274165", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23274165", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23274165", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23274166/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23274166/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23274166/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23274166/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23274166:gaussian-propeller-stability.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23274166:gaussian-propeller-stability.pdf/full/%5E50,/0/default.jpg", "100": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23274166:gaussian-propeller-stability.pdf/full/%5E100,/0/default.jpg", "250": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23274166:gaussian-propeller-stability.pdf/full/%5E250,/0/default.jpg", "750": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23274166:gaussian-propeller-stability.pdf/full/%5E750,/0/default.jpg", "1200": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23274166:gaussian-propeller-stability.pdf/full/%5E1200,/0/default.jpg"}, "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23274166/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23274166/latest", "versions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23274166/versions", "draft": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23274166/draft", "access_links": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23274166/access/links", "access_grants": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23274166/access/grants", "access_users": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23274166/access/users", "access_request": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23274166/access/request", "access": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23274166/access", "communities": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23274166/communities", "communities-suggestions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23274166/communities-suggestions", "request_deletion": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23274166/request-deletion", "file_modification": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23274166/file-modification", "quota_increase": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23274166/quota-increase", "requests": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23274166/requests"}, "updated": "2026-10-12T03:53:34.718937+00:00", "recid": "23274166", "revision": 4, "files": [{"id": "06a5691b-aac5-4783-954b-d9c668fd3800", "key": "gaussian-propeller-stability-arxiv-source.zip", "size": 10736, "checksum": "md5:f3ec7a679814ceae29f7a91bdcfe2216", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23274166/files/gaussian-propeller-stability-arxiv-source.zip/content"}}, {"id": "a3bc83ae-81c0-4e76-bd0a-c9774cde5ffe", "key": "gaussian-propeller-stability.pdf", "size": 114056, "checksum": "md5:496ae779a50608bf8d1dd7a0cda6272f", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23274166/files/gaussian-propeller-stability.pdf/content"}}], "swh": null, "owners": [{"id": "1931625"}], "status": "published", "stats": {"downloads": 4, "unique_downloads": 4, "views": 2, "unique_views": 2, "version_downloads": 4, "version_unique_downloads": 4, "version_unique_views": 2, "version_views": 2}, "state": "done", "submitted": true}, {"created": "2026-10-25T17:35:31.360399+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-25T17:35:32.529020+00:00", "id": 23647118, "conceptrecid": "23647117", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23647118", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23647117", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23647118", "metadata": {"title": "Spectral chart selection and average trace-class distortion", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23647118", "publication_date": "2026-10-25", "description": "<p>We construct genuine finite negative-type metrics with n points whose first uniform-average distortion into the trace class S_1(H) is at least c sqrt(log n)/(log log n)^(9/2), uniformly over all complex Hilbert spaces H. The construction uses the multichart Hilbert kernel of the stipulated pinned uniform-sparsest-cut source. A dimension-independent matrix selection replaces scalar coordinate selection: scalar moment matching supplies spectral cutoffs, and a positive Gaussian dual pairing averages them without requiring commutation. The argument tracks chart count, rounding mesh and triangle repair; finite-rank compression, Hermitian dilation and uniform copies preserve the full statement. The final release includes attribution corrections and bounded primary-reading limits. Worldwide priority is not claimed.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>AI-assisted preprint by Myeongjin Kang, with no affiliation. Internal AI review is not external journal peer review or worldwide-priority certification. Identified OpenAI source inputs at revision fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb are stipulated true. Lean verifies scoped supporting results only, not the full theorem. Original prose: CC BY 4.0; original code and Lean: MIT; third-party rights preserved. See the supporting archive for precise assumptions, coverage, provenance and corrections.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Kang, Myeongjin", "affiliation": null}], "version": "1.0", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23647117"}}]}}, "title": "Spectral chart selection and average trace-class distortion", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23647118", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23647118", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23647118?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23647118", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23647118", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23647118", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23647118/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23647117", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23647117", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23647117", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23647117", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23647118/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23647118/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23647118/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23647118/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23647118:r038-main.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23647118:r038-main.pdf/full/%5E50,/0/default.jpg", "100": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23647118:r038-main.pdf/full/%5E100,/0/default.jpg", "250": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23647118:r038-main.pdf/full/%5E250,/0/default.jpg", "750": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23647118:r038-main.pdf/full/%5E750,/0/default.jpg", "1200": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23647118:r038-main.pdf/full/%5E1200,/0/default.jpg"}, "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23647118/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23647118/latest", "versions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23647118/versions", "draft": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23647118/draft", "access_links": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23647118/access/links", "access_grants": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23647118/access/grants", "access_users": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23647118/access/users", "access_request": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23647118/access/request", "access": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23647118/access", "communities": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23647118/communities", "communities-suggestions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23647118/communities-suggestions", "request_deletion": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23647118/request-deletion", "file_modification": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23647118/file-modification", "quota_increase": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23647118/quota-increase", "requests": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23647118/requests"}, "updated": "2026-10-25T17:35:32.529020+00:00", "recid": "23647118", "revision": 3, "files": [{"id": "ccb7a2fc-5b49-42b4-bdf8-ed3c964d1bf0", "key": "r038-t117q-local-release.zip", "size": 493918, "checksum": "md5:f57ef615707c76c0f8f709510a7f58ec", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23647118/files/r038-t117q-local-release.zip/content"}}, {"id": "7af358b1-6a06-4f08-b81b-b2fd7f25b778", "key": "r038-main.pdf", "size": 161087, "checksum": "md5:f961e8b19ce9f4de3f0700b41a91975c", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23647118/files/r038-main.pdf/content"}}], "swh": null, "owners": [{"id": "1931625"}], "status": "published", "stats": {"downloads": 0, "unique_downloads": 0, "views": 0, "unique_views": 0, "version_downloads": 0, "version_unique_downloads": 0, "version_unique_views": 0, "version_views": 0}, "state": "done", "submitted": true}, {"created": "2026-10-25T17:36:22.959053+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-25T17:36:23.394195+00:00", "id": 23647127, "conceptrecid": "23647126", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23647127", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23647126", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23647127", "metadata": {"title": "Projection-body volume for four-dimensional polytopes with at most six facets", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23647127", "publication_date": "2026-10-25", "description": "<p>For every convex four-dimensional polytope K with nonempty interior and at most six actual facets, we prove V_4(&Pi;K) &le; (160/3)V_4(K)^3, with equality precisely for simplices. The projection body is normalized by h_{&Pi;K}(u) = V_3(K projected onto u-perpendicular) for unit u. Under the identified stipulated source interfaces, an attained simplex-section maximum reduces the six-facet case to a signed sum of four independent exponential variables. Log-concavity and Laplace comparison and a two-bracket identity reduce the estimate to ten explicit polynomial certificates. Repeated knots, zero coefficients and nonsimple polytopes are included. No claim is made for seven or more facets, general four-dimensional bodies or dimensions five through eight.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>AI-assisted preprint by Myeongjin Kang, with no affiliation. Internal AI review is not external journal peer review or worldwide-priority certification. Identified OpenAI source inputs at revision fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb are stipulated true. Lean verifies scoped supporting results only, not the full theorem. Original prose: CC BY 4.0; original code and Lean: MIT; third-party rights preserved. See the supporting archive for precise assumptions, coverage, provenance and corrections.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Kang, Myeongjin", "affiliation": null}], "version": "1.0", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"